ctlStampProbe -- SEQ 193 1b: P4's certificate, measured on TODAY's stamped binary (H16).

NOT A FLEET ROW. It is the evidence for the stop: the two rows the plan names do not
discriminate, and two other positions do.

Measured 2026-09-26 on parse-then-fire at 72d89bc + the isBrancH accessor, stamp intact:
  PLAN-1 return x: returned value            7
  PLAN-1 return x: x isBranch                0   <- plan wants 0 AFTER P4; reads 0 BEFORE too
  PLAN-2 failed operand: false isBranch      0   <- same
  LEAK loop over a returning callee ran      3
  CAND-1 continue v: v isBranch              2   <- the stamp OUTLIVES, interpreted road
  CAND-1 continue v: loop ran                2   (its non-zero sibling)
  CAND-2 jit-compiled return w: w isBranch   3   <- the stamp OUTLIVES the compile, jitted road

WHY THE PLAN ROWS ARE VOID: processAction ends `if result = result.gMethod(result)
result.isBranch = 0;` (GroupActions.rtn:596) -- the action boundary already clears the
stamp off the value it hands back, so `return x;` and the falseResult it may return are
clean by the time anything can read them. An H7 "restore the stamp -> red" cannot fire.
WHERE THE STAMP SURVIVES: a loop consumes `continue` by replacing the result with
trueResult and never clears the stamped node, so `continue v;` leaves v at 2; and under
jitting aCTionBlocK `continue`s past the branch and the compile has no processAction
frame, so the emit-time stamp on the operand stays at 3.
